{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261002T014554Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "b9f92f4f287905ab9fdbef77", "title": "Build Applications on NVIDIA BlueField Faster with NVIDIA DOCA Agent Skills", "url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/build-applications-on-nvidia-bluefield-faster-with-nvidia-doca-agent-skills/", "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog", "published": "2026-10-01T18:13:29+00:00", "is_ai": 0.75, "worthiness": 0.745, "worthiness_confidence": 0.93, "final_score": 0.745, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 10374, "delivered": true, "summary": "NVIDIA released DOCA AI agent skills on GitHub—domain-specific knowledge packs that equip AI agents with verified APIs, hardware requirements, and build constraints for BlueField DPU development. Without skills, agents failed 81% of real DOCA tasks (misusing APIs, skipping hardware checks, wrong tool routing); with skills, they achieved 100% success across 65 test prompts. The key takeaway: structured domain knowledge lets agents generate correct code immediately rather than through trial-and-error cycles, reducing handwritten code by 73% and hardware commands by 46% in real workflows.", "jev_ms": 206.6, "jev_input_tokens": 2793, "jev_cost": 0.000117306, "llm_ms": 2701.3, "llm_cost": 0.003216, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261002T014554Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "bc7ec3e2a0e4be9f03cd4752", "title": "Build Local AI Apps with C++ and NVIDIA TensorRT RTX Samples", "url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/build-local-ai-apps-with-c-and-nvidia-tensorrt-rtx-samples/", "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog", "published": "2026-10-01T17:59:27+00:00", "is_ai": 0.98, "worthiness": 0.74, "worthiness_confidence": 0.96, "final_score": 0.74, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 3645, "delivered": true, "summary": "NVIDIA released DIN Deploy, an open-source C++ sample collection combining ONNX Runtime with TensorRT RTX for building hardware-accelerated local AI applications on Windows and Linux. It demonstrates practical workflows for ASR (Whisper, Parakeet), image segmentation (SAM 2.1), and image generation (FLUX.2), with GPU acceleration delivering 38-206x speedups over CPU. The key takeaway: use ONNX as a portable format with vendor-specific acceleration isolated to optional paths, enabling model-agnostic deployment code that works across hardware targets via CMake presets.", "jev_ms": 176.9, "jev_input_tokens": 1452, "jev_cost": 6.0984e-05, "llm_ms": 2838.8, "llm_cost": 0.001801, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261002T014554Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "1fca9693a1dac487012f67c2", "title": "Fine-Tuning NVIDIA Nemotron for Saudi Arabic Dialects, with a Path to Other Languages", "url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/fine-tuning-nvidia-nemotron-for-saudi-arabic-dialects-with-a-path-to-other-languages/", "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog", "published": "2026-10-01T05:00:00+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.85, "worthiness_confidence": 0.64, "final_score": 0.85, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 17798, "delivered": true, "summary": "NVIDIA released a fine-tuning guide for Nemotron 3.5 ASR to adapt multilingual speech recognition to Saudi Arabic dialects (Najdi, Hijazi) while retaining English and Modern Standard Arabic. Key techniques include minimal curation (keeping 82.5% of data), weighted replay mixing (90% target, 10% FLEURS), and duration-based bucketing, which reduced SADA WER from 55% to 30% in 4.5 hours on two GPUs without degrading English performance. The workflow prevents catastrophic forgetting during dialect specialization and generalizes to other low-resource languages by adjusting corpus metadata, normalization, and evaluation metrics accordingly.", "jev_ms": 199.0, "jev_input_tokens": 5287, "jev_cost": 0.000222054, "llm_ms": 3448.6, "llm_cost": 0.005886, "errors": []}
